{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Suddenly.</b> Rashi explained: He revealed Himself to them suddenly while they were ritually impure (טמאין בדרך ארץ), and they were crying out 'water, water' — to let them know that Moshe acted well in separating from his wife, since the Shekhinah was revealed upon him constantly and there was no fixed time for speech." "<b>And there are</b> those who explain פתאם as 'suddenly,' so that they would not turn back — for in this their speech there was desecration of HaShem (חלול ה׳), for all who speak disparagingly of the prophets are as if speaking against the Shekhinah, and desecration of HaShem is among the severe transgressions that hold back repentance, and this is the sense of פתאם — before they turn back in repentance, in the manner of what was said: 'there is no encompassing (מקיפין) in the case of desecration of HaShem,' from the mouth of my master and teacher, Rabbi Nathan, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:47.624455084Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}